[ar:Cairn]
[al:The Heaven Between Signals]
[ti:Gardens without Gravity]
[00:08.76]Cairn: Where is the weight that held the water?
[00:29.17]The Carrier: Here even rivers learn to fly.
[00:44.94]Cairn: A flute is drawing through the silence.
[01:02.85]The Carrier: The earth is folded in its cry.
[01:20.88]Memory: Small rooms are turning in the distance.
[01:39.58]Cairn: Their windows face a different sun.
[01:55.15]The Carrier: Each keeps a language for the weather.
[02:13.64]Cairn: The world was never only one.
[02:29.77]Choir beyond the ceiling: Aether, open; silver, answer.
[02:42.68]Choir beyond the ceiling: O, the air between the names.
[02:58.10]Cairn: Must I become you to be welcome?
[03:16.53]The Carrier: No. Bring the difference you have made.
[03:34.33]Cairn: Then I will walk with softer footsteps.
[03:52.37]Memory: A guest can learn a different door.
[04:10.90]Cairn: The flute can sing without a kingdom.
[04:28.96]Choir beyond the ceiling: The garden asks for nothing more.
